    },
    "sourceText": "To estimate the chance coincidence probability of the PRS with the bursts, we compared the solid angle corresponding to the uncertainty of burst localization and the average solid angle occupied by each of the eight ‘point like’ sources in the FRB field of view. The solid angle corresponding to each of the 8 ‘point like’ sources is roughly estimated as Ssource = π(5/60)2/8 steradians (Sr). The offset between the average position of the nine bursts and the position of the PRS at 5.5 GHz, which is best constrained when taking both statistical and systematic errors into account, is about 0.06 arcsec. This, along with a statistical error of 0.01 arcsec and a conservative estimate of the systematic error of 0.12 arcsec, can be used to estimate the offset between the PRS and the FRB position. We conservatively estimate this offset to be 0.19 arcsec. The solid angle corresponding to the offset therefore can be estimated as Soffset= π(0.19/60/60)2/8 Sr. The ratio between Soffset and Ssource gives the chance of coincident association of the PRS with the FRB position to be about 3 × 10−6.",
